# .gitignore — project-scoped ignores only.
#
# Personal / environment ignores (IDE, OS, editor swap files, personal
# backups) are intentionally NOT listed here so they leave no trace in
# the project. Put those in your own global excludes file instead:
#
#   git config --global core.excludesFile ~/.gitignore
#
# This file covers only what every contributor must ignore regardless of
# their machine: build output, secrets, runtime caches, logs, content
# deliberately kept out of the public source tree, and the one stray
# OS artefact (.directory) that tends to litter many folders at once.

# ---- GitHub community-health files (force-tracked) ----
# A personal global excludesFile (~/.gitignore) may ignore .github/ wholesale.
# Re-include the directory here so this project's own community files —
# CODEOWNERS, the issue-template chooser, workflows, dependabot — always track
# for every contributor, regardless of their machine's global ignores.
!.github/

# ---- Maven ----
target/
pom.xml.tag
pom.xml.releaseBackup
pom.xml.versionsBackup
pom.xml.next
release.properties
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
buildNumber.properties
.mvn/timing.properties
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# ---- Quarkus ----
.quarkus/
quarkus-app/

# ---- Native build artefacts ----
*-runner
*-runner.jar
*-runner.exe
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib

# ---- Local config that may carry secrets ----
# Profile-scoped application*.{properties,yml} are committed (template form);
# a local override is not. Real cert paths and broker / Miniserver credentials
# live in the operator's deployment, never in version control.
src/main/resources/application-local.properties
src/main/resources/application-local.yaml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Logs / JFR ----
log/
logs/
jfr/
*.jfr
*.log

# ---- LoxAPP3 cache (loxone.miniserver.cache.directory) ----
# Populated at runtime when the bridge fetches data/LoxAPP3.json from a real
# Miniserver. Default location is ./cache relative to CWD. Never tracked.
cache/

# ---- Coverage / test artefacts ----
.scannerwork/
coverage/

# ---- Runtime sockets / lock files ----
*.lock
*.pid

# ---- KDE Dolphin folder metadata ----
# Normally a personal/global ignore, but .directory spawns in many folders
# at once, so the project ignores it centrally (the one OS-artefact exception).
.directory
